<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!-- ⛔ TEMPORARY, DEBUG VARIANT ONLY (09/10/2026, Anthuan's request).
         Exists for the BENCH PROBE: during testing, the app sends each scan's diagnostic
         to the VPS, and CC reads it in real time instead of him sending a screenshot per screen.

         Why this file and not the main manifest: Gradle merges the manifest PER VARIANT.
         Being here, the release APK is born WITHOUT android.permission.INTERNET by
         construction, not by the discipline of whoever remembers to remove it later. The
         alternative (declaring it in main and guarding the code with if BuildConfig.DEBUG)
         keeps the permission declared on the published app's listing. Unacceptable for an
         accessibility app that promises to send nothing out, and it's exactly the price
         Binspector paid in its privacy policy.

         This build does NOT go to the Play Store or anywhere else: it's a test bench.
         When mapping wraps up, this disappears along with nginx's /sonda/ location. -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />

</manifest>
